 the public\nL116:       * cite1†Information for Media L117:       * cite2†Services of the CZSO for the public L118:       * cite84†We popularise statistics L119:       * cite85†Awards of the CZSO L120:     * cite86†Anti-Corruption Efforts L121:     * Compulsory disclosure information\nL122:       * cite87†Official Notice Board L123:       * cite88†Information provided under Act No 106/1999 Sb on Free Access to Information L124:       * cite89†Personal data protection (GDPR) L125: Search\nL126: \nL127:   * cite7†Czech Statistical Office L128:   * cite90†Statistics L129:   * cite91†Economy L130:   * cite25†Prices, inflation L131:   * cite92†Inflation, Consumer Prices L132:   * cite93†Notes to consumer prices of energy L133:   * Note to consumer prices of energy - October 2023\nL134: # Note to consumer prices of energy - October 2023\nL135: \nL136:   *   *   *   *   *\nL137: \nL138: For period October 2022 – December 2022, the so-called Saving tariff was introduced for households purchasing electricity.\nL139: For period October 2022 – December 2023, the fee for supported energy sources (POZE) was waived.\nL140: Saving tariff – subsidy for the payment of energy costs for household customers – was introduced by government decree (No. 262/2022 Coll. of August 24, 2022) for the months of October to December 2022. The amount of the contribution was determined by the distribution rate negotiated at the take-off points of household customers, where the contribution was taken into account.\nL141: The total amount allocated to this \"tariff\" was published in the press release of the Ministry of Finance (\"Implementation of the state budget of the Czech Republic for October 2022\", dated November 1, 2022).\nL142: Fee for supported energy sources (POZE) – was waived from October 2022 to December 2023. Price Decision of the Energy Regulatory Office No. 8/2022 of September 2, 2022 was released for October to December 2022, Price Decision of the Energy Regulatory Office No. 13/2022 of November 14, 2022 for January to December 2023.\nL143: Consumer price index without including influence of Saving tariff for households would have in October reached a value 105.8% (instead of 108.5%), year-on-year, of which for electricity 124.7% (instead of 248.6%).\nL144: \nL145: Detailed explanation of the methodology for including the Savings Tariff and waiving POZE in Detailed methodology explanation of the inclusion of Saving tariff and POZE waiver in a calculation of consumer price index was published together with News release for October 2022.\nL146:   * cite90†Statistics L147:   * cite94†Databases, applications L148:   * cite95†Methodology L149:   * cite96†Data collection L150:   * cite97†About us L151: ## Top searched\nL152: \nL153:   * cite0†Contact L154:   * cite56†Public database†vdb.czso.cz L155:   * cite55†DataStat (trial run)†data.csu.gov.cz L156:   * cite1†Media L157:   * cite54†Journals L158:   * cite2†Services L159:   * cite4†Catalogue of Products L160:   * cite3†Events L161:   * cite5†Regional offices L162: \nL163: ## Data protection and Legislation\nL164: \nL165:   * cite98†Cookies and web analytics L166:   * cite99†Conditions of Use L167:   * cite89†Privacy policy L168:   * cite100†Accessibility L169: \nL170:   * cite101†Site map L171: \nL172: ## We recommend\nL173: \nL174:   * cite61†Mobile application L175: ## Social Media\nL176: \nL177:   *   *   *   *   *\nL178: \nL179:   * © Czech Statistical Office | 2026\nL180:   * Latest update: 09. 11. 2023\n"
